module

public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.TensorCoherence
public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.TensorExactnessSheafify
public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Sites.DenseSubsite.SheafEquiv

/-!
# Restriction of finite data to a slice site, with no products on the site

Let `R` be a sheaf of rings on a site `(C, J)` and let `x` be an object of `C`. Restriction
`SheafOfModules.overFunctor R x` to the slice site over `x` is a left adjoint as soon as `C` has
binary products, because the right adjoint is built from `CategoryTheory.Over.star`; that is how
`SheafOfModules.Presentation.map`, `SheafOfModules.GeneratingSections.map` and
`SheafOfModules.mapFreeIso` are usually fed the colimit preservation they ask for. A site in the
sense of the Stacks project (Tag 00VH) is not assumed to have products, so every statement proved
that way is weaker than its source.

This file removes that hypothesis for **finite** data, which is all that finiteness statements
about sheaves of modules ever need. Restriction is an additive functor between preadditive
categories, so it preserves finite coproducts unconditionally; a finite presentation or a finite
family of generating sections involves only finite coproducts and one cokernel, and the cokernel
is handled by transporting the colimit along the finite free comparison rather than by asking the
functor to preserve it. The net effect is products-free analogues of `Presentation.map`,
`GeneratingSections.map` and `Presentation.quasicoherentData`, and a products-free form of Stacks
Tag 01BP for a target with a local finite presentation.

The file also records that the twice iterated slice hypotheses which Mathlib's
`SheafOfModules.QuasicoherentData.bind` and this project's
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.LocalKernel.isFiniteType_of_coversTop` carry are **not** extra hypotheses:
they follow from the once sliced ones, because `CategoryTheory.Over.iteratedSliceEquiv` is an
equivalence of sites.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.SliceFinite.freeOverIso`: for a finite index type, the comparison
  `free I ≅ (free I).over x`, built from additivity instead of from an adjunction.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.SliceFinite.sliceGenerators`: the restriction to the slice site over `x`
  of a finite family of generating sections.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.SliceFinite.slicePresentation`: the restriction to the slice site over
  `x` of a finite presentation, with `Stacks.SheafOfModules.SliceFinite.sliceKernelIso`
  identifying the restricted kernel with the kernel of the restricted generating morphism.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.SliceFinite.quasicoherentDataOfPresentation`: the quasi-coherent data on
  the trivial cover attached to a finite global presentation. This is Mathlib's
  `SheafOfModules.Presentation.quasicoherentData` without `HasBinaryProducts C`.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.SliceFinite.localGeneratorsDataOfEpi`: local generators pushed forward
  along an epimorphism.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.SliceFinite.alphaOf` and `betaOf`: the two comparison morphisms of the
  Stacks 01BP argument, as in
  `Stacks.SheafOfModules.FiniteTypeKernel.alphaOf`/`betaOf` but with a finite index type and no
  products.

## Main results

* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.SliceFinite.epi_overFunctor_map`: restriction to a slice site preserves
  epimorphisms. This is local surjectivity restricted to a slice
  (`Stacks.TensorCoherence.isLocallySurjective_overWhisker'`), not colimit preservation, so it
  needs no products.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.SliceFinite.preservesColimitsOfShape_discrete_overFunctor`: restriction
  to a slice site preserves coproducts indexed by a finite type.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.SliceFinite.isFinitePresentation_of_presentation`: a sheaf of modules
  with a finite global presentation is of finite presentation.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.SliceFinite.isFiniteType_of_epi`: a quotient of a sheaf of modules of
  finite type is of finite type. This is `Stacks.SheafOfModules.isFiniteType_of_epi` without
  `HasBinaryProducts C`.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.SliceFinite.hasSheafify_iteratedSlice` and
  `wEqualsLocallyBijective_iteratedSlice`: the twice iterated slice sheafification hypotheses
  follow from the once sliced ones.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.SliceFinite.isFiniteType_kernel_of_presentation`: Stacks Tag 01BP for a
  target with a finite global presentation, with no products on the site.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.SliceFinite.isFiniteType_kernel_of_generatingSections`: **Stacks Tag
  01BP** for a target of finite presentation and a source generated by finitely many *global*
  sections, with no products and no pullbacks on the site.

## Implementation notes

**Why finite coproducts are free.** `SheafOfModules.pushforward` is additive on the nose: its
action on morphisms is `PresheafOfModules.pushforward` applied to the underlying morphism of
presheaves of modules, and that is precomposition with a functor followed by restriction of
scalars, so `map (f + g) = map f + map g` holds by `rfl`. Mathlib's
`CategoryTheory.Functor.preservesFiniteCoproductsOfAdditive` then gives preservation of
coproducts indexed by a `Fin n`, and `preservesColimitsOfShape_of_equiv` transports that to an
arbitrary finite index type. Nothing here is a size or smallness condition, and nothing uses the
adjunction `SheafOfModules.overPushforwardOverAdj`.

**Why the cokernel is free too.** `SheafOfModules.Presentation.map` asks for
`PreservesColimitsOfSize`, which restriction to a slice site has only through that adjunction.
The construction here never maps the cokernel: the restricted generating morphism is *defined* as
`freeOverIso.hom ≫ overFunctor.map σ.π`, its epimorphy comes from `epi_overFunctor_map`, and the
kernel of the restriction is identified with the restriction of the kernel by
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.FiniteTypeKernel.preservesLimitPushforward`, which holds for any
continuous functor. So only finite coproducts are ever mapped.

**The iterated slice hypotheses.** For `Z : Over U` the equivalence
`CategoryTheory.Over.iteratedSliceEquiv : Over Z ≌ Over Z.left` is an equivalence of sites
between `(J.over U).over Z` and `J.over Z.left`; Mathlib records its inverse as an
`IsDenseSubsite`. Transporting `HasSheafify` is then
`CategoryTheory.Equivalence.hasSheafify`, and transporting `WEqualsLocallyBijective` is
`CategoryTheory.GrothendieckTopology.WEqualsLocallyBijective.transport`, which additionally wants
limits over the comma categories `StructuredArrow X G.op`. Those exist for a trivial reason:
`G` is an equivalence, so each of those comma categories has an initial object, and a diagram
whose source has an initial object has a limit. That is `hasInitial_structuredArrow`.

**Duplication.** `alphaOf`, `betaOf`, `isFiniteType_kernel_of_presentation`,
`localGeneratorsDataOfEpi` and `isFiniteType_of_epi` repeat
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.FiniteTypeKernel.alphaOf`, `betaOf`,
`isFiniteType_kernel_of_presentation`, `Stacks.SheafOfModules.localGeneratorsDataOfEpi` and
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.isFiniteType_of_epi` with `HasBinaryProducts C` dropped and `Finite` added
on the index types where the proof needs it.

**Universes.** The site `C : Type u₁` has `Category.{v₁} C` and the sheaf of rings is
`R : Sheaf J RingCat.{u}` with `u`, `u₁`, `v₁` unrelated, which is the generality in which
Mathlib states `SheafOfModules.IsFiniteType` and `SheafOfModules.IsFinitePresentation`. Nothing
is specialised.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01BP](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01BP)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01BD](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01BD)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 00VH](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00VH)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory Limits SheafOfModules Opposite

universe u v₁ u₁

namespace Stacks.SheafOfModules.SliceFinite

/-! ### Restriction to a slice site preserves epimorphisms and finite coproducts -/

section Basic

variable {C : Type u₁} [Category.{v₁} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C} {Rs : Sheaf J RingCat.{u}}

/-- Restriction of sheaves of modules to a slice site is additive. -/
instance additive_overFunctor (x : C) : (overFunctor.{u} Rs x).Additive where
  map_add := by intros; rfl

variable [HasSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{u}] [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]

/-- **Restriction to a slice site preserves epimorphisms.** An epimorphism of sheaves of modules
is locally surjective, local surjectivity restricts to a slice site, and a locally surjective
morphism of sheaves of modules is an epimorphism. No products on the site are needed. -/
instance epi_overFunctor_map {M N : SheafOfModules.{u} Rs} (p : M ⟶ N) [Epi p] (x : C) :
    Epi ((overFunctor Rs x).map p) :=
  Stacks.SheafOfModules.EpiMono.epi_of_isLocallySurjective _
    (Stacks.TensorCoherence.isLocallySurjective_overWhisker' J _ x
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.EpiMono.isLocallySurjective_of_epi p))

variable [∀ X : C, HasSheafify (J.over X) AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ X : C, (J.over X).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]

/-- **Restriction to a slice site preserves coproducts indexed by a finite type.** It is an
additive functor between preadditive categories, hence preserves finite biproducts, and in a
preadditive category a finite biproduct is a finite coproduct. -/
instance preservesColimitsOfShape_discrete_overFunctor (x : C) (I : Type u) [Finite I] :
    PreservesColimitsOfShape (Discrete I) (overFunctor.{u} Rs x) := by
  obtain ⟨n, ⟨e⟩⟩ := Finite.exists_equiv_fin I
  have := (inferInstance : PreservesFiniteCoproducts (overFunctor.{u} Rs x)).preserves n
  exact preservesColimitsOfShape_of_equiv (Discrete.equivalence e.symm) _

/-- Restriction to a slice site takes the unit sheaf of modules to the unit sheaf of modules, on
the nose. The type must be ascribed: the two spellings are definitionally equal and are not
interchangeable for `rw`. -/
noncomputable def unitOverIso (x : C) :
    unit (Rs.over x) ≅ (overFunctor.{u} Rs x).obj (unit Rs) :=
  Iso.refl _

/-- The restriction to the slice site over `x` of the free sheaf of modules on a finite index
type, as a comparison isomorphism. -/
noncomputable def freeOverIso (x : C) (I : Type u) [Finite I] :
    (free I : SheafOfModules.{u} (Rs.over x)) ≅ (overFunctor.{u} Rs x).obj (free I) :=
  mapFreeIso (overFunctor.{u} Rs x) I (unitOverIso x)

/-- The comparison `freeOverIso` sends the `i`-th basis section of the free sheaf of modules on the
slice site to the restriction of the `i`-th basis section. -/
@[reassoc (attr := simp)]
lemma ιFree_freeOverIso_hom (x : C) (I : Type u) [Finite I] (i : I) :
    ιFree i ≫ (freeOverIso (Rs := Rs) x I).hom = (overFunctor Rs x).map (ιFree i) := by
  show ιFree i ≫ (mapFreeIso (overFunctor.{u} Rs x) I (unitOverIso x)).hom = _
  rw [ιFree_mapFreeIso_hom]
  exact Category.id_comp _

end Basic

/-! ### Restriction of generating sections and of a presentation -/

section Restrict

variable {C : Type u₁} [Category.{v₁} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C} {Rs : Sheaf J RingCat.{u}}
  [HasSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{u}] [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ X : C, HasSheafify (J.over X) AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ X : C, (J.over X).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  {M : SheafOfModules.{u} Rs}

/-- The restriction to the slice site over `x` of a finite family of generating sections. -/
noncomputable def sliceGenerators (σ : M.GeneratingSections) [σ.IsFiniteType] (x : C) :
    (M.over x).GeneratingSections where
  I := σ.I
  s := (M.over x).freeHomEquiv ((freeOverIso x σ.I).hom ≫ (overFunctor Rs x).map σ.π)
  epi := by rw [Equiv.symm_apply_apply]; exact epi_comp _ _

/-- The generating morphism of `sliceGenerators σ x` is the comparison `freeOverIso` followed by
the restriction of the generating morphism of `σ`. -/
lemma sliceGenerators_π (σ : M.GeneratingSections) [σ.IsFiniteType] (x : C) :
    (sliceGenerators σ x).π = (freeOverIso x σ.I).hom ≫ (overFunctor Rs x).map σ.π :=
  (M.over x).freeHomEquiv.symm_apply_apply _

/-- The restriction of a finite family of generating sections is finite. -/
instance sliceGenerators_isFiniteType (σ : M.GeneratingSections) [σ.IsFiniteType] (x : C) :
    (sliceGenerators σ x).IsFiniteType :=
  ⟨inferInstanceAs (Finite σ.I)⟩

/-- Local generators data pushed forward along an epimorphism, with no products on the site:
the covering is unchanged and each generating family is replaced by the family of its images. -/
noncomputable def localGeneratorsDataOfEpi {N : SheafOfModules.{u} Rs}
    (σ : M.LocalGeneratorsData) (p : M ⟶ N) [Epi p] : N.LocalGeneratorsData where
  I := σ.I
  X := σ.X
  coversTop := σ.coversTop
  generators i := (σ.generators i).ofEpi ((overFunctor Rs (σ.X i)).map p)

/-- Local generators data of finite type pushed forward along an epimorphism is of finite type. -/
instance localGeneratorsDataOfEpi_isFiniteType {N : SheafOfModules.{u} Rs}
    (σ : M.LocalGeneratorsData) (p : M ⟶ N) [Epi p] [h : σ.IsFiniteType] :
    (localGeneratorsDataOfEpi σ p).IsFiniteType where
  isFiniteType i :=
    have := h.isFiniteType i
    inferInstanceAs ((σ.generators i).ofEpi ((overFunctor Rs (σ.X i)).map p)).IsFiniteType

/-- A quotient of a sheaf of modules of finite type is of finite type. This is
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.isFiniteType_of_epi` without `HasBinaryProducts C`. -/
theorem isFiniteType_of_epi {N : SheafOfModules.{u} Rs} (p : M ⟶ N) [Epi p]
    (hM : M.IsFiniteType) : N.IsFiniteType := by
  obtain ⟨σ, hσ⟩ := hM.exists_localGeneratorsData
  exact { exists_localGeneratorsData :=
    Exists.intro (localGeneratorsDataOfEpi σ p) inferInstance }

/-- The restriction to the slice site over `x` of the kernel of the generating morphism is the
kernel of the restricted generating morphism: restriction preserves limits, and a kernel does not
change under precomposition with an isomorphism. -/
noncomputable def sliceKernelIso (σ : M.GeneratingSections) [σ.IsFiniteType] (x : C) :
    (overFunctor Rs x).obj (kernel σ.π) ≅ kernel (sliceGenerators σ x).π :=
  PreservesKernel.iso (overFunctor Rs x) σ.π ≪≫
    (kernelIsIsoComp (freeOverIso x σ.I).hom ((overFunctor Rs x).map σ.π)).symm ≪≫
      eqToIso (by rw [sliceGenerators_π]; rfl)

/-- The restriction to the slice site over `x` of a finite presentation. This is Mathlib's
`SheafOfModules.Presentation.map` along `SheafOfModules.overFunctor`, built without assuming
that the site has binary products. -/
noncomputable def slicePresentation (P : M.Presentation) [P.IsFinite] (x : C) :
    (M.over x).Presentation where
  generators := sliceGenerators P.generators x
  relations := (sliceGenerators P.relations x).ofEpi (sliceKernelIso P.generators x).hom

/-- The restriction of a finite presentation is finite. -/
instance slicePresentation_isFinite (P : M.Presentation) [P.IsFinite] (x : C) :
    (slicePresentation P x).IsFinite where
  isFiniteType_generators := ⟨inferInstanceAs (Finite P.generators.I)⟩
  isFiniteType_relations := ⟨inferInstanceAs (Finite P.relations.I)⟩

/-- The quasi-coherent data on the trivial cover attached to a finite global presentation. This
is Mathlib's `SheafOfModules.Presentation.quasicoherentData` without `HasBinaryProducts C`. -/
noncomputable def quasicoherentDataOfPresentation (P : M.Presentation) [P.IsFinite] :
    M.QuasicoherentData where
  I := C
  X := id
  coversTop x := GrothendieckTopology.covering_of_eq_top J <| by
    rw [Sieve.ext_iff]
    intro _ f
    simp [Sieve.top_apply]
  presentation x := slicePresentation P x

/-- The quasi-coherent data attached to a finite global presentation consists of finite
presentations. -/
instance quasicoherentDataOfPresentation_isFinitePresentation (P : M.Presentation) [P.IsFinite] :
    (quasicoherentDataOfPresentation P).IsFinitePresentation where
  isFinite_presentation x := slicePresentation_isFinite P x

/-- **A sheaf of modules with a finite global presentation is of finite presentation.** -/
theorem isFinitePresentation_of_presentation (P : M.Presentation) [P.IsFinite] :
    M.IsFinitePresentation :=
  ⟨⟨quasicoherentDataOfPresentation P, inferInstance⟩⟩

end Restrict

/-! ### The twice iterated slice hypotheses are not extra hypotheses -/

section Iterated

/-- For an equivalence `T`, every comma category `StructuredArrow X T` has an initial object: the
structural arrow attached to the isomorphism `T.obj (T.objPreimage X) ≅ X`. -/
theorem hasInitial_structuredArrow {D E : Type*} [Category* D] [Category* E] (T : D ⥤ E)
    [T.IsEquivalence] (X : E) : HasInitial (StructuredArrow X T) :=
  let h : IsInitial ((StructuredArrow.mapIso (T := T) (T.objObjPreimageIso X)).functor.obj
      (StructuredArrow.mk (Y := T.objPreimage X) (𝟙 (T.obj (T.objPreimage X))))) :=
    (StructuredArrow.mkIdInitial (T := T)).isInitialObj _ _
  h.hasInitial

variable {C : Type u₁} [Category.{v₁} C] (J : GrothendieckTopology C)

/-- **Sheafification on a twice iterated slice site.** `Over.iteratedSliceEquiv` identifies the
site `((J.over U).over Z)` with the site `J.over Z.left`. -/
theorem hasSheafify_iteratedSlice [∀ X : C, HasSheafify (J.over X) AddCommGrpCat.{u}] (U : C)
    (Z : Over U) : HasSheafify ((J.over U).over Z) AddCommGrpCat.{u} :=
  Equivalence.hasSheafify ((J.over U).over Z) (J.over Z.left) Z.iteratedSliceEquiv _

/-- **Local bijectivity on a twice iterated slice site.** -/
theorem wEqualsLocallyBijective_iteratedSlice
    [∀ X : C, HasSheafify (J.over X) AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
    [∀ X : C, (J.over X).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}] (U : C) (Z : Over U) :
    ((J.over U).over Z).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u} := by
  have hlim : ∀ X : (Over Z)ᵒᵖ,
      HasLimitsOfShape (StructuredArrow X Z.iteratedSliceEquiv.inverse.op) AddCommGrpCat.{u} :=
    fun X => { has_limit := fun _ =>
      let := hasInitial_structuredArrow Z.iteratedSliceEquiv.inverse.op X
      inferInstance }
  exact GrothendieckTopology.WEqualsLocallyBijective.transport ((J.over U).over Z)
    (J.over Z.left) Z.iteratedSliceEquiv.inverse (Functor.IsDenseSubsite.coverPreserving _ _ _)

end Iterated

/-! ### Stacks Tag 01BP without products on the site -/

section Kernel

variable {C : Type u₁} [Category.{v₁} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C} {Rs : Sheaf J RingCat.{u}}
  [HasSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{u}] [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ X : C, HasSheafify (J.over X) AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ X : C, (J.over X).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]

/-- The comparison morphism `α` of the Stacks 01BP argument, assembled over `V` from local lifts
of the generators of the source through the presentation of the target. -/
noncomputable def alphaOf {n Iγ : Type u} [Finite n] (V : C)
    (τ : Iγ → (unit (Rs.over V) ⟶ (free (R := Rs) n).over V)) :
    free (R := Rs.over V) Iγ ⟶ free (R := Rs.over V) n :=
  (freeHomEquiv _).symm fun k => (free (R := Rs.over V) n).unitHomEquiv
    (τ k ≫ (freeOverIso V n).inv)

/-- `alphaOf` is a lift of the generating morphism of the source through the presentation. -/
lemma alphaOf_spec {n Iγ : Type u} [Finite n] [Finite Iγ] {F G : SheafOfModules.{u} Rs}
    (θ : G ⟶ F) (V : C) (φ₀ : free (R := Rs) n ⟶ F) (γ₀ : free (R := Rs) Iγ ⟶ G)
    (τ : Iγ → (unit (Rs.over V) ⟶ (free (R := Rs) n).over V))
    (hτ : ∀ k, τ k ≫ φ₀.over V =
      (show unit (Rs.over V) ⟶ F.over V from (ιFree k ≫ γ₀ ≫ θ).over V)) :
    alphaOf (Rs := Rs) V τ ≫ ((freeOverIso V n).hom ≫ φ₀.over V) =
      ((freeOverIso V Iγ).hom ≫ γ₀.over V) ≫ θ.over V := by
  refine FiniteTypeKernel.free_hom_ext fun k => ?_
  simp only [Category.assoc, alphaOf, FiniteTypeKernel.ιFree_freeHomEquiv_symm_assoc,
    Equiv.symm_apply_apply, Iso.inv_hom_id_assoc, ιFree_freeOverIso_hom_assoc]
  rw [hτ k]
  exact (overFunctor Rs V).map_comp _ _

/-- The comparison morphism `β` of the Stacks 01BP argument, assembled over `V` from local lifts
of the presentation generators of the target through `θ`. -/
noncomputable def betaOf {n : Type u} {G : SheafOfModules.{u} Rs} (V : C)
    (υ : n → (unit (Rs.over V) ⟶ G.over V)) :
    free (R := Rs.over V) n ⟶ G.over V :=
  (freeHomEquiv _).symm fun l => (G.over V).unitHomEquiv (υ l)

/-- `betaOf` is a lift of the presentation of the target through `θ`. -/
lemma betaOf_spec {n : Type u} [Finite n] {F G : SheafOfModules.{u} Rs} (θ : G ⟶ F) (V : C)
    (φ₀ : free (R := Rs) n ⟶ F) (υ : n → (unit (Rs.over V) ⟶ G.over V))
    (hυ : ∀ l, υ l ≫ θ.over V =
      (show unit (Rs.over V) ⟶ F.over V from (ιFree l ≫ φ₀).over V)) :
    betaOf (Rs := Rs) V υ ≫ θ.over V = (freeOverIso V n).hom ≫ φ₀.over V := by
  refine FiniteTypeKernel.free_hom_ext fun l => ?_
  simp only [betaOf, FiniteTypeKernel.ιFree_freeHomEquiv_symm_assoc, Equiv.symm_apply_apply,
    ιFree_freeOverIso_hom_assoc]
  rw [hυ l]
  exact (overFunctor Rs V).map_comp _ _

/-- Over an object `V` where the generators of `G` lift through the presentation of `F`, and the
presentation generators of `F` lift through `θ`, the restriction of `kernel θ` to the slice site
over `V` is generated by finitely many sections. -/
lemma exists_generatingSections_over {F G : SheafOfModules.{u} Rs}
    (P : F.Presentation) [P.IsFinite] (gs : G.GeneratingSections) [gs.IsFiniteType]
    (θ : G ⟶ F) (V : C)
    (τ : gs.I → (unit (Rs.over V) ⟶ (free (R := Rs) P.generators.I).over V))
    (hτ : ∀ k, τ k ≫ (P.generators.π).over V =
      (show unit (Rs.over V) ⟶ F.over V from (ιFree k ≫ gs.π ≫ θ).over V))
    (υ : P.generators.I → (unit (Rs.over V) ⟶ G.over V))
    (hυ : ∀ l, υ l ≫ θ.over V =
      (show unit (Rs.over V) ⟶ F.over V from (ιFree l ≫ P.generators.π).over V)) :
    ∃ σ : ((kernel θ).over V).GeneratingSections, Finite σ.I := by
  set PV := slicePresentation P V with hPV
  set gsV := sliceGenerators gs V with hgsV
  have hα : alphaOf (Rs := Rs) V τ ≫ PV.generators.π = gsV.π ≫ θ.over V := by
    simp only [PV, gsV, slicePresentation, sliceGenerators_π]
    exact alphaOf_spec θ V _ _ τ hτ
  have hβ : betaOf (Rs := Rs) V υ ≫ θ.over V = PV.generators.π := by
    simp only [PV, slicePresentation, sliceGenerators_π]
    exact betaOf_spec θ V _ υ hυ
  have hχφ : ((freeHomEquiv _).symm PV.relations.s ≫ kernel.ι PV.generators.π) ≫
      PV.generators.π = 0 := by simp
  have h1 : Finite PV.relations.I := inferInstanceAs (Finite P.relations.I)
  have h2 : Finite gsV.I := inferInstanceAs (Finite gs.I)
  refine ⟨GeneratingSections.equivOfIso (PreservesKernel.iso (overFunctor Rs V) θ).symm
    (FiniteTypeKernel.generatingSectionsKernel
      ((freeHomEquiv _).symm PV.relations.s ≫ kernel.ι PV.generators.π) gsV.π
      (alphaOf (Rs := Rs) V τ) (betaOf (Rs := Rs) V υ) PV.generators.π (θ.over V)
      hχφ hα hβ PV.isColimit), ?_⟩
  exact inferInstanceAs (Finite (PV.relations.I ⊕ gsV.I))

/-- **Stacks Tag 01BP for a target with a finite global presentation, with no products on the
site.** If `F` admits a finite presentation by global sections and `θ : G ⟶ F` is an epimorphism
from a sheaf of modules generated by finitely many global sections, then `Ker θ` is of finite
type. -/
theorem isFiniteType_kernel_of_presentation {F G : SheafOfModules.{u} Rs}
    (P : F.Presentation) [P.IsFinite] (gs : G.GeneratingSections) [gs.IsFiniteType]
    (θ : G ⟶ F) [Epi θ] : (kernel θ).IsFiniteType := by
  classical
  have hcover : J.CoversTop (Subtype.val :
      { V : C // ∃ σ : ((kernel θ).over V).GeneratingSections, Finite σ.I } → C) := by
    intro Y
    choose S₁ hS₁ hlift₁ using fun k : gs.I =>
      FiniteTypeKernel.exists_lift_over_of_epi P.generators.π (ιFree k ≫ gs.π ≫ θ) Y
    choose S₂ hS₂ hlift₂ using fun l : P.generators.I =>
      FiniteTypeKernel.exists_lift_over_of_epi θ (ιFree l ≫ P.generators.π) Y
    refine J.superset_covering ?_
      (J.intersection_covering (FiniteTypeKernel.iInf_mem J _ hS₁)
        (FiniteTypeKernel.iInf_mem J _ hS₂))
    intro V g hg
    obtain ⟨hg₁, hg₂⟩ := hg
    rw [FiniteTypeKernel.iInf_apply] at hg₁ hg₂
    choose τ hτ using fun k => hlift₁ k g (hg₁ k)
    choose υ hυ using fun l => hlift₂ l g (hg₂ l)
    exact (Sieve.mem_ofObjects_iff _ g).2
      ⟨⟨V, exists_generatingSections_over P gs θ V τ hτ υ hυ⟩, ⟨𝟙 V⟩⟩
  exact ⟨⟨{ I := { V : C // ∃ σ : ((kernel θ).over V).GeneratingSections, Finite σ.I }
            X := Subtype.val
            coversTop := hcover
            generators := fun i => i.2.choose }, ⟨fun i => ⟨i.2.choose_spec⟩⟩⟩⟩

/-- **Stacks Tag 01BP, with no products and no pullbacks on the site.** If `F` is of finite
presentation and `θ : G ⟶ F` is an epimorphism from a sheaf of modules generated by finitely many
*global* sections, then `Ker θ` is of finite type.

Because the generators of the source are global, the covering family on which the target has a
finite presentation needs no refinement, so the restriction of a presentation along a morphism of
the site — the step that needs `HasPullbacks C` in
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.LocalKernel.kernel_isFiniteType_of_epi_from_finiteType` — never
occurs. -/
theorem isFiniteType_kernel_of_generatingSections {F G : SheafOfModules.{u} Rs}
    [F.IsFinitePresentation] (gs : G.GeneratingSections) [gs.IsFiniteType] (θ : G ⟶ F) [Epi θ] :
    (kernel θ).IsFiniteType := by
  have hs2 : ∀ (X : C) (Z : Over X), HasSheafify ((J.over X).over Z) AddCommGrpCat.{u} :=
    fun X Z => hasSheafify_iteratedSlice J X Z
  have hs3 : ∀ (X : C) (Z : Over X),
      ((J.over X).over Z).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u} :=
    fun X Z => wEqualsLocallyBijective_iteratedSlice J X Z
  obtain ⟨q, hq⟩ := IsFinitePresentation.exists_quasicoherentData F
  refine LocalKernel.isFiniteType_of_coversTop (kernel θ) q.X q.coversTop fun i => ?_
  have hP := hq.isFinite_presentation i
  have hker : (kernel (θ.over (q.X i))).IsFiniteType :=
    isFiniteType_kernel_of_presentation (q.presentation i) (sliceGenerators gs (q.X i))
      (θ.over (q.X i))
  exact isFiniteType_of_epi (PreservesKernel.iso (overFunctor Rs (q.X i)) θ).inv hker

end Kernel

end Stacks.SheafOfModules.SliceFinite

